      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start, but honestly, the citation density is still pretty low. The tracking system is going to flag this as \"low rigor\" if we don't get that score up more. \n\nCould you expand on this? I need a much more detailed version. Specifically, can you go into more detail on the economic projections and the environmental mitigation for the wetlands? \n\nPlease try to sink in as many actual academic or governmental citations as you can find to back up these points—it's really important for the committee that the document looks heavily researched. Just, like I said before, please make sure they are legitimate sources. I'd rather have fewer real ones than extra fake ones, but we definitely need a much higher density than what's here.",
